# Open this file in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
# Click "Send Request" above each block, top to bottom.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### 1. Log in (seeded admin from appsettings.Development.json)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@example.com", "password": "ChangeMe123!" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### 2. Create a project (comes with development + production environments)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "key": "demo-shop", "name": "Demo Shop" }

### 3. Create a boolean flag
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/demo-shop/flags
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "key": "new-checkout", "name": "New checkout", "description": "Redesigned checkout flow", "kind": "Boolean" }

### 4. Read it back (copy the variation ids and each environment's version from the response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/demo-shop/flags/new-checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Turn it on in development. Replace the GUIDs and expectedVersion with values from step 4.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/demo-shop/flags/new-checkout/environments/development
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enabled": true,
  "offVariationId": "REPLACE-WITH-FALSE-VARIATION-ID",
  "fallthrough": { "rollout": [
    { "variationId": "REPLACE-WITH-TRUE-VARIATION-ID",  "weight": 2000 },
    { "variationId": "REPLACE-WITH-FALSE-VARIATION-ID", "weight": 8000 }
  ] },
  "rules": [
    {
      "description": "Premium users",
      "clauses": [ { "attribute": "plan", "op": "eq", "values": ["premium"] } ],
      "serve": { "variationId": "REPLACE-WITH-TRUE-VARIATION-ID" }
    }
  ],
  "expectedVersion": 1
}

### 6. Send step 5 again unchanged: expectedVersion is now stale, so you should get 409
### 7. Audit log for the project
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/demo-shop/audit?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Create a server SDK key for production (the plaintext key is shown only once)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/demo-shop/environments/production/sdk-keys
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "Server" }
